	"visibility"		"0"
	"title"		"Viewpoint Extended Support"
	"description"		"[h1]Viewpoint Extended Support[/h1] Quality-of-life and compatibility features for Project Viewpoint in Project Zomboid Build 42.20+. [h2]Viewpoint features[/h2][list][*]Automatically switch to third person when entering vehicles and return to first person after exiting.[*]Toggle first/third person with a configurable bind (default: Shift+Z); binds support Shift, Ctrl, Alt, and combinations.[*]Hold Mouse Button 4 for free mouse control, with optional automatic cursor support for inventories and menus, including Ergonomic UI.[*]Hide the Viewpoint interaction menu while the vanilla or Ergonomic UI inventory is open (enabled by default and configurable).[*]Adjust third-person camera distance using the mouse wheel or configurable keys (default: minus and equals).[*]Optional cascading interaction menus with deferred [i]View options[/i] loading.[*]Preserves vanilla interaction icons and optionally integrates with Simple Context Menu Icons.[*]Optionally enter Viewpoint automatically when starting a game and skip the startup setup screen.[/list][h2]Project A-Life and Companion Dogs[/h2][list][*]A-Life NPC interaction actions are available from Viewpoint's interaction menu.[*]Aiming at an A-Life NPC displays its name tag above the NPC.[*]Companion Dogs name tags are correctly positioned with Viewpoint's camera.[*]When Companion Dogs is installed, Friendly and Allied A-Life NPCs are excluded from the dog's threat detection.[/list][h2]Requirements[/h2][list][*]Project Viewpoint[*]ZombieBuddy 2.3.0 or newer[*]Project Zomboid Build 42.20+[*]Project A-Life is optional and required only for its NPC features.[/list][h2]Configuration[/h2] Customize features and key binds in the in-game Mod Options. Firearm aiming and weapon behavior remain handled by Project Viewpoint. [h2]Mod information[/h2][list][*]Mod Name: ViewpointExtendedSupport[*]Mod ID: 3812978679[/list]"
	"changenote"		"Add A-Life NPC interactions and aimed tags; improve Companion Dogs tag and threat compatibility."
}
